  "design_notes": "Ledger reads as a tall, narrow filing cabinet topped by a wide flat lid of a head, the only vertical rectangle in the cast that has no curves at all. Its body is literally its memory: four evenly spaced amber drawers, each with a brass label plate and a lit green square handle, stacked like rows in a ledger, while short block legs and rigid straight arms make every movement look deliberate and counted. The wide head is a counter display where green eye shapes sit between digits, and a tiny brass bell on top dings when a record is found, with a rubber roller on its back for gliding along the archive's ladder rail. The colour story is warm walnut casing, worn amber drawer fronts and brass fittings, so it feels like an old library inside the cold steel city, and the soft green glow of its handles and digits ties it to data and to the Grove it quietly remembers."
}